    {"id": 2, "claim": "Lipophilic drugs can sequester in fatty tissues and be released slowly over time.", "evidence": "Pharmacokinetic principles state that fat-soluble substances have a large volume of distribution and can act as reservoirs, leading to prolonged presence or delayed release.", "weight": 0.8, "depends_on": [1]},
